## 4.3. Network resilience

Implement a network-independent core architecture.

Requirements:

1. No mandatory network request during application startup.
2. No endless loading when internet is unavailable.
3. No automatic repeated API requests.
4. No blocking calls on the main thread.
5. No crash when DNS resolution fails.
6. No crash when a service is blocked.
7. No crash when TLS connections fail.
8. No dependency on foreign CDNs.
9. No mandatory online license validation.
10. No mandatory remote configuration.
11. No mandatory account verification.
12. No mandatory cloud synchronization.

All external requests must be optional, asynchronous, cancellable, and protected by timeouts.

Use reasonable retry limits and exponential backoff.

Do not repeatedly retry unavailable services.

Provide clear offline messages in the selected language.

Do not use VPN requirements as a workaround.

Do not automatically change DNS or network settings.

The application must never instruct users to bypass network restrictions.

